# Scheduled-only policy/VLA-private Global -> Pipeline close protocol.
# session_id (UUID4) and logical_generation identify the Global logical session.
# binding_id (UUID4), positive binding_incarnation, and expected_boot_id (UUID4)
# must match the accepted Open, including for cleanup with zero generations.
# operation_id is the downstream operation UUID4 and is echoed in the result.
# Ledger key: (session_id, operation_id). Duplicate identity/payload must
# be unchanged (including operation_id); duplicates wait/replay retained results.
# A different deadline does not extend an existing Close. NOT_STARTED allows
# retry; UNKNOWN is not proof of drain and must retain cleanup ownership.
# A new operation_id starts a cleanup attempt only when the binding controller
# allows Close; an active Close is rejected and all attempts use the drain barrier.
# Close cancellation is rejected. Caller timeout does not stop the drain.
# success=true guarantees this binding's work is fenced and drained through the
# whole-graph reset barrier, or that no cleanup was needed. A terminal action or
# COMPLETED outcome alone does not guarantee successful drain; check success.
string<=36 session_id
# Positive logical generation, or zero to select the current bound generation
# during cleanup of a late/failed Open whose result was not obtained.
uint64 logical_generation
string<=36 binding_id
uint64 binding_incarnation
string<=36 operation_id
string<=36 expected_boot_id
# Positive Open result generation, or zero for cleanup when it is unknown.
uint64 expected_pipeline_generation
# Required positive absolute UTC Unix deadline, never ROS/simulation time.
# Zero is invalid; Global resolves defaults before sending this private action.
builtin_interfaces/Time deadline
---
bool success
string<=36 session_id
uint64 logical_generation
string<=36 binding_id
uint64 binding_incarnation
string<=36 operation_id
string<=36 boot_id
string<=63 pipeline_id
# Closed product generation and reset/drain fence generation, respectively.
# Zero is possible for cleanup with no active product or no cleanup needed.
# On failure these fields are diagnostic, not evidence that drain succeeded.
# Normal success requires drained_generation > closed_pipeline_generation > 0.
# The only zero/zero success is cleanup_not_needed for a generation-zero request.
uint64 closed_pipeline_generation
uint64 drained_generation
ibrobot_msgs/InferenceOutcome outcome
ibrobot_msgs/ScheduledInferenceError error
---
string<=128 status
